<title>JAPAN: SHOWA YOKKAICHI SAYS HALTS CRUDE UNIT DUE TO FIRE.</title>
<headline>SHOWA YOKKAICHI SAYS HALTS CRUDE UNIT DUE TO FIRE.</headline>
<dateline>TOKYO 1997-08-11</dateline>
<text>
<p>Showa Yokkaichi Sekiyu has halted operations at its 150,000 barrel per day (BPD) crude distillation unit (CDU) at Yokkaichi, in central Japan's Mie Prefecture, a plant official said on Monday.</p>
<p>The official said the closure was caused by a fire at the unit which was quickly extinguished. The official added that the unit would remain closed until safety inspectors could examine the site on Tuesday and assess the damage.</p>
</text>
